title: Law on the Referendum
new-page: true
choose-if: party_resources > 0 and parlament_sovereignty_declaration and ((erc_roadmap > 1 and player_party = "erc") or (cup_roadmap > 1 and player_party = "cup")) and not parlament_referendum_law and (speaker_party = "jxsi" or speaker_party = "erc" or speaker_party = "cup" or speaker_party = "jxcat" or speaker_party = "junts" or speaker_party = "dl" or speaker_party = "pdecat" or speaker_party = "cdc" or (speaker_party = "csqp" and csqp_leader = "Arcadi Oliveres") or (speaker_party = "cecp" and cecp_leader = "Arcadi Oliveres") or (speaker_party = "cecp" and cecp_leader = "Jaume Asens"))
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament) {
        Q.party_resources -= 1;
    } else {
        // Penalty for not being the one to propose it?
    }

    if (!Q.unio_split && Q.ciu_roadmap <= 1) {
        Q.roadmaps_card_ciu_reach += 1;
    }
    if (Q.player_party != "erc" && Q.erc_roadmap <= 1){
        Q.roadmaps_card_erc_reach += 1;
    }
    Q.parlament_referendum_saw_ciu = 0;
    Q.parlament_current_ciu_roadmap = Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_roadmap"];

    // TODO: what happens on favourable Spanish government?
!}
unavailable-subtitle: [? if parlament_referendum_law : Already approved! ?][? if (not parlament_referendum_law) and ((erc_roadmap <= 1 and player_party = "erc") or (cup_roadmap <= 1 and player_party = "cup")) : Our roadmap to independence is about achieving an agreement with the Spanish government. ?][? if (not parlament_referendum_law) and (not parlament_sovereignty_declaration) : A parlamentary Declaration of Sovereignty is required first. ?][? if (not parlament_referendum_law) and (party_resources < 1) : Not enough resources. ?][? if (not parlament_referendum_law) and not (speaker_party = "jxsi" or speaker_party = "erc" or speaker_party = "cup" or speaker_party = "jxcat" or speaker_party = "junts" or speaker_party = "dl" or speaker_party = "pdecat" or speaker_party = "cdc" or (speaker_party = "csqp" and csqp_leader = "Arcadi Oliveres") or (speaker_party = "cecp" and cecp_leader = "Arcadi Oliveres") or (speaker_party = "cecp" and cecp_leader = "Jaume Asens")) : Speaker of the House [+ speaker +] ([+ speaker_party +]) will not allow debating this.?]
subtitle: [? if coming_from_parlament : \[-1 resources\] ?]
go-to: default_choices

= Law on the Referendum

[? if parlament_non_binding_consultations: Unlike the previously-approved Law on Non-Binding Consultations, our?][? if not parlament_non_binding_consultations: Our?] lawmakers are now proposing a new framework that would compel the President to call for a legally-binding referendum on the political status of Catalonia. While its constitutional fit would be hard to defend, and more so without an agreement with the central government, the Parlament's Sovereignty Declaration could be used as a basis instead. 

The truly complex topic, however, is the part about making the result legally binding. In case a result favouring independence, there a legal path needs to be built and ready for Catalonia to transition from an Autonomous Community to a fully-fledge independent state. The proposal: the accompanying Law of Juridical transition and foundation of the Republic, which should establish the framework for administrations to assume broader powers, functioning as interim foundational law while the Constitution of the Catalan Republic is drafted an approved. 

[? if not unio_split: CiU is currently urging us not to pursue this path at the moment, as the UDC wing is not willing to walk these steps. ?][? if president_party = "ciu": [? if president_gender = "m": President ?][? if president_gender = "f": Presidenta ?][+ president +] is not currently endorsing this path, so it may be difficult to actually enforce these twin laws. ?][? if president != "Arcadi Oliveres" and (president_party = "csqp" or president_party = "cecp" or president_party = "ecp" or president_party = "psc" or president_party = "cs" or president_party = "ppc" or president_party = "vox"): [? if president_gender = "m": President ?][? if president_gender = "f": Presidenta ?][+ president +] is very much against this path of action, and will most definitely work against the enforcement of these laws. ?]

@default_choices

- @non_binding
- @proceed
- @ups_go_back

@non_binding
title: Wait this sounds too serious, let's do a Non-Binding Consultation instead
view-if: coming_from_parlament
choose-if: not parlament_non_binding_consultations
unavailable-subtitle: The Law on Non-Binding Consultations has already been approved!
subtitle: It may be better to play it safe after all
go-to: parlament_non_binding_consultations

@ups_go_back
title: Wait let's not do this...
subtitle: Our lawmakers can focus on another law after all
view-if: coming_from_parlament and parlament_non_binding_consultations
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.coming_from_parlament) {
        Q.party_resources += 1;
    }
    Q.independence_trust -= 5;
!}
go-to: parlament_card.sovereignty

@proceed
title: Let's get this done!
subtitle: [? if parlament_referendum_saw_ciu: CiU is very probably going to hold this against us. ?][? if parlament_referendum_saw_erc: Without even the votes from ERC, there's a chance this gets brushed off as some sort of as an "unrealistic" CUP chicanery. ?]
choose-if: player_party != "erc" or (erc_pragmatic_strength < 30 and erc_roadmap < 3)
unavailable-subtitle: The pragmatics within our party currently enjoy a position of strength, and are currently skeptical in thinking this may be the best course of action.
go-to: ciu_sure if (not unio_split or parlament_current_ciu_roadmap <= 1) and not parlament_referendum_saw_ciu; erc_sure if not player_party = "erc" and erc_roadmap <= 1 and not parlament_referendum_saw_erc; vote

@ciu_sure
on-arrival: parlament_referendum_saw_ciu = 1
go-to: default_choices

[? if president_party = parlament_current_ciu: [? if president_gender = "m": President ?][? if president_gender = "f": Presidenta ?][+ president +] is strongly insisting that this is not the way, at least not yet. ?]
[? if parlament_current_ciu = "ciu": With an ambiguous position and a difficult internal balance, CiU is really not in a position to endorse this path of action. ?]All in all, we may want to reconsider this. Not only unitary voting in the Parlament may be in peril, but pro-independence unity all together.

Are we completely sure we want to proceed?

@erc_sure
on-arrival: parlament_referendum_saw_erc = 1
go-to: default_choices

ERC is currently defending a [+ erc_roadmap : roadmap +] roadmap to independence, and that puts them in a bit of a tight spot for this vote. While not necessarily against one such law eventually, they are right now prioritizing an agreement with the central government, and are urging us to not move forward with this path just yet. 

[? if parlament_referendum_saw_ciu: Once again, are?][? if not parlament_referendum_saw_ciu: Are?] we completely sure we want to proceed?

@vote
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0) { 
        // TBD: too harsh?
        Q.ciu_relations = Math.min(29, Q.ciu_relations -= 10);
    } 
    if (Q.erc_parlament_s > 0 && Q.erc_roadmap <= 1 && Q.player_party != "erc") {
        Q.erc_relations = Math.min(39, Q.erc_relations -= 10);
    }
    Q.independence_movement += 5;
    // Q.independence_movement = Math.max(80, Q.independence_movement + 5);

    Q.parlament_referendum_yes = Q.cup_parlament_s + Q.jxsi_parlament_s + Q.jxcat_parlament_s + Q.fnc_parlament_s;
    Q.parlament_referendum_abst = Q.icv_parlament_s;
    Q.parlament_referendum_no = Q.ecp_parlament_s + Q.pxc_parlament_s;
    Q.parlament_referendum_notpresent = 0;

    var yes_parties = [];
    var abstain_parties = [];
    var not_present_parties = [];
    var no_parties = [];
    function add_if_seated(list, label, seats, count) {
        if (seats <= 0) {
            return;
        }
        var party = { label: label };
        if (count !== undefined && count !== null) {
            party.count = count;
        }
        list.push(party);
    }

    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "JxSí", Q.jxsi_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "JxCat", Q.jxcat_parlament_s);

    if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0) {
        var ciu_abst = Math.min(Math.round(Q.ciu_parlament_s * 0.67), Q.ciu_parlament_s - 1);
        var ciu_no = Math.max(Math.round(Q.ciu_parlament_s * 0.33), 1);
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += ciu_abst;
        Q.parlament_referendum_no += ciu_no;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "CiU", Q.ciu_parlament_s, ciu_abst);
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "CiU", Q.ciu_parlament_s, ciu_no);
    } else if (Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_roadmap"] > 1 && !(Q.jxsi_formed && !Q.jxsi_dissolved) && !(Q.jxcat_formed && !Q.jxcat_dissolved)) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_yes += Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"];
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, Q.parlament_current_ciu, Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"]);
    } else if (Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_roadmap"] <= 1 && !(Q.jxsi_formed && !Q.jxsi_dissolved) && !(Q.jxcat_formed && !Q.jxcat_dissolved)) {
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, Q.parlament_current_ciu, Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"]);
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"];
    }
    
    if (Q.player_party == "erc" || Q.erc_roadmap > 1) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_yes += Q.erc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "ERC", Q.erc_parlament_s);
    } else {
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += Q.erc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "ERC", Q.erc_parlament_s);
    }

    if (Q.psc_leader == "Àngel Ros" || Q.psc_leader == "Núria Parlon") {
        Q.parlament_referendum_no += Q.psc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
    } else if (Q.psc_leader == "Montserrat Tura") {
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += Q.psc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
    } else {
        if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0 || (Q.erc_roadmap <= 1 && Q.erc_parlament_s > 0)) {
            Q.parlament_referendum_no += Q.psc_parlament_s;
            add_if_seated(no_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
        } else {
            Q.parlament_referendum_notpresent += Q.psc_parlament_s;
            add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
        }
    }


    if (Q.csqp_leader == "Arcadi Oliveres" && Q.csqp_parlament_s > 0) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_yes += Q.csqp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CSQP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    } else if ((Q.cecp_leader == "Arcadi Oliveres" || Q.cecp_leader == "Jaume Asens") && Q.cecp_parlament_s > 0) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_yes += Q.cecp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CECP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    } else {
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += Q.cecp_parlament_s + Q.csqp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "CECP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "CSQP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    }

    add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "ICV-EUiA", Q.icv_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(no_parties, "ECP", Q.ecp_parlament_s);

    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CUP", Q.cup_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "FNC", Q.fnc_parlament_s);

    if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0 || (Q.erc_roadmap <= 1 && Q.erc_parlament_s > 0)) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_no += Q.ppc_parlament_s + Q.cs_parlament_s + Q.vox_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "Cs", Q.cs_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "PPC", Q.ppc_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "Vox", Q.vox_parlament_s);
    } else {
        Q.parlament_referendum_notpresent += Q.ppc_parlament_s + Q.cs_parlament_s + Q.vox_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "Cs", Q.cs_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "PPC", Q.ppc_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "Vox", Q.vox_parlament_s);
    }
    add_if_seated(no_parties, "PxC", Q.pxc_parlament_s);

    Q.parlament_referendum_vote_result = {
        outcomes: [
            {
                kind: "yes",
                label: "Yes",
                votes: Q.parlament_referendum_yes,
                parties: yes_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "abstain",
                label: "Abstention",
                votes: Q.parlament_referendum_abst,
                parties: abstain_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "not-present",
                label: "Not Present",
                votes: Q.parlament_referendum_notpresent,
                parties: not_present_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "no",
                label: "No",
                votes: Q.parlament_referendum_no,
                parties: no_parties
            }
        ]
    };

    if (Q.parlament_referendum_yes > Q.parlament_referendum_no) {
        Q.parlament_referendum_law = true;
        G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"referendum_law",title:"Law on the Referendum ",icon:"img/government_icon.svg", targets:{independence_movement: 0.2, independence_trust: 0.1}});
        Q.burdens_done += 1;
    } else {
        Q.parlament_referendum_law = false;
        Q.independence_trust -= 10;
    }
    Q.coming_from_parlament = false;
!}

<div data-widget="chamber-vote" data-props='{"configFrom":"parlament_referendum_vote_result"}'></div>

[? if parlament_referendum_law: After a marathon-legth session of the Parlament[? if parlament_referendum_notpresent > 0: , and with opposition parties leaving half-way, refusing to even partake in the final vote,?] the Law on the Referendum has been passed! ?][? if not parlament_referendum_law: It seems like, despite all our efforts, the Law on the Referendum will not come to be, at least this time around. ?][? if ciu_parlament_s > 0: Even if unusal, there has been a rather predicatble split in the CiU vote, where CDC has abstained while UDC has voted against it. ?]

The session has been intense to say the least, with oposition parties fuming at even such a debate even being allowed. Speaker of the House [+ speaker +] has been the one to receive most of that hate after allowing an alteration to the agenda to include the vote[? if speaker_gender = "f" : , including very nasty mysoginistic comments against her?]. [? if parlament_referendum_law and ((csqp_parlament_s > 0 and csqp_leader != "Arcadi Oliveres") or (cecp_parlament_s > 0 and cecp_leader != "Arcadi Oliveres") or ecp_parlament_s > 0 or icv_parlament_s > 0): [+ parlament_current_icv +] has also had their stellar moment when Joan Coscubiela has equated the vote to outright vote fraud.?] All in all, not the brightest day for the Parlament.

- @next_law
- @try_again


@try_again
title: We'll be retrying this!
subtitle: A bit more unity on the pro-independence front may be required...
view-if: not parlament_referendum_law
go-to: post_event

@next_law
title: and we're not done yet
view-if: parlament_referendum_law
new-page: true

= Law of Juridical transition and foundation of the Republic

The second of the twin laws on *"disconnection"* is very much a necessity to make the "binding" part of a referendum actually binding. While indeed the proposed law would fill the void between an independence declaration and the establishment of a new Catalan Constitution, the interim foundational law is, of course, even more controversial than the one regarding the Referendum. From its basis on the Declaration of Sovereigty and not the Spanish Constition, the opposition is very much ready to rule it out as completely unusable. On the flip side, it is not without criticism from the pro-independence front, as it would give the Catalan Republic a very presidentialist system during this interim period. 

In any case, and with the parliamentary session already running late into the night, the moment is here.

- @pre_law

@pre_law
title: Speaker of the House [+ speaker +] orders the agenda to include the vote of the second *"disconnection"* law
face-image: img/events/filldaniel.png

As the Parlament votes on changing the agenda, the oposition explodes in protest. Insults are thrown around, and Joan Coscubiela ([+ parlament_current_icv +]), is again the portagonist of the moment. *"I don't want my son, Daniel, to live in a country where a majority can step on the rights of those who don't think like them*, he says, comparing the current situation with Franco-era repression he and his family fought against. Surreally, most of his own party do **not** applaud his speech, leaving him to receive a standing ovation from Cs[? if vox_parlament_s > 0: , vox?][? if psc_leader = "Miquel Iceta": , the PSC?], and the PPC.

After that and a few more explosive speeches by [+ cs_leader +] and [+ ppc_leader +], the oposition leaves the chambers in protest. Left behind, a few Spanish flags, promptly picked up and put away by some [+ parlament_current_icv +] MPs.

- @transition_law

@transition_law
title: Let's wrap this up!
on-arrival: {!
    Q.parlament_disconnection_yes = Q.cup_parlament_s + Q.jxsi_parlament_s + Q.jxcat_parlament_s + Q.fnc_parlament_s;
    Q.parlament_disconnection_abst = 0;
    Q.parlament_disconnection_no = Q.ecp_parlament_s + Q.pxc_parlament_s + Q.icv_parlament_s;
    Q.parlament_disconnection_notpresent = 0;

    var yes_parties = [];
    var abstain_parties = [];
    var not_present_parties = [];
    var no_parties = [];
    function add_if_seated(list, label, seats, count) {
        if (seats <= 0) {
            return;
        }
        var party = { label: label };
        if (count !== undefined && count !== null) {
            party.count = count;
        }
        list.push(party);
    }

    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "JxSí", Q.jxsi_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "JxCat", Q.jxcat_parlament_s);

    if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0) {
        var ciu_abst = Math.min(Math.round(Q.ciu_parlament_s * 0.67), Q.ciu_parlament_s - 1);
        var ciu_no = Math.max(Math.round(Q.ciu_parlament_s * 0.33), 1);
        Q.parlament_disconnection_abst += ciu_abst;
        Q.parlament_disconnection_no += ciu_no;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "CiU", Q.ciu_parlament_s, ciu_abst);
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "CiU", Q.ciu_parlament_s, ciu_no);
    } else if (Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_roadmap"] > 1 && !(Q.jxsi_formed && !Q.jxsi_dissolved) && !(Q.jxcat_formed && !Q.jxcat_dissolved)) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_yes += Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"];
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, Q.parlament_current_ciu, Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"]);
    } else if (Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_roadmap"] <= 1 && !(Q.jxsi_formed && !Q.jxsi_dissolved) && !(Q.jxcat_formed && !Q.jxcat_dissolved)) {
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, Q.parlament_current_ciu, Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"]);
        Q.parlament_disconnection_abst += Q[Q.parlament_current_ciu + "_parlament_s"];
    }
    
    if (Q.player_party == "erc" || Q.erc_roadmap > 1) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_yes += Q.erc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "ERC", Q.erc_parlament_s);
    } else {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_abst += Q.erc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "ERC", Q.erc_parlament_s);
    }

    if (Q.psc_leader == "Àngel Ros" || Q.psc_leader == "Núria Parlon") {
        Q.parlament_referendum_no += Q.psc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
    } else if (Q.psc_leader == "Montserrat Tura") {
        Q.parlament_referendum_abst += Q.psc_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
    } else {
        if (Q.ciu_parlament_s > 0 || (Q.erc_roadmap <= 1 && Q.erc_parlament_s > 0)) {
            Q.parlament_referendum_no += Q.psc_parlament_s;
            add_if_seated(no_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
        } else {
            Q.parlament_referendum_notpresent += Q.psc_parlament_s;
            add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "PSC", Q.psc_parlament_s);
        }
    }

    if (Q.csqp_leader == "Arcadi Oliveres" && Q.csqp_parlament_s > 0) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_yes += Q.csqp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CSQP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    } else if ((Q.cecp_leader == "Arcadi Oliveres") && Q.cecp_parlament_s > 0) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_yes += Q.cecp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CECP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    } else if ((Q.cecp_leader == "Jaume Asens") && Q.cecp_parlament_s > 0) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_abst += Q.cecp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(abstain_parties, "CECP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    } else {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_no += Q.cecp_parlament_s + Q.csqp_parlament_s;
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "CECP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
        add_if_seated(no_parties, "CSQP", Q.cecp_parlament_s);
    }

    add_if_seated(no_parties, "ICV-EUiA", Q.icv_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(no_parties, "ECP", Q.ecp_parlament_s);

    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "CUP", Q.cup_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(yes_parties, "FNC", Q.fnc_parlament_s);


    Q.parlament_disconnection_notpresent += Q.ppc_parlament_s + Q.cs_parlament_s + Q.vox_parlament_s;
    add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "Cs", Q.cs_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "PPC", Q.ppc_parlament_s);
    add_if_seated(not_present_parties, "Vox", Q.vox_parlament_s);

    add_if_seated(no_parties, "PxC", Q.pxc_parlament_s);

    Q.parlament_disconnection_vote_result = {
        outcomes: [
            {
                kind: "yes",
                label: "Yes",
                votes: Q.parlament_disconnection_yes,
                parties: yes_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "abstain",
                label: "Abstention",
                votes: Q.parlament_disconnection_abst,
                parties: abstain_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "not-present",
                label: "Not Present",
                votes: Q.parlament_disconnection_notpresent,
                parties: not_present_parties
            },
            {
                kind: "no",
                label: "No",
                votes: Q.parlament_disconnection_no,
                parties: no_parties
            }
        ]
    };

    if (Q.parlament_disconnection_yes > Q.parlament_disconnection_no) {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_law = true;
        Q.burdens_done += 1;
        G.registerLaw(Q, {id:"transition_law",title:"Law of Juridical Transition",icon:"img/scales_icon.svg", targets:{independence_movement: 0.2, independence_trust: 0.1, cat_spa_relations: -0.1}});
    } else {
        Q.parlament_disconnection_law = false;
        Q.independence_trust -= 10;
        Q.not_possible_parlament_stuck = true;
    }
!}

<div data-widget="chamber-vote" data-props='{"configFrom":"parlament_disconnection_vote_result"}'></div>

